  i am allowed to tell you this i can't  actually talk to you guys about my quest  that's a spoiler i'm not allowed to go  into details about that because i am  an npc um with what i think is a pretty  dope quest  but worth noting i am only available in  the nomad playthrough  which is part of why i keep saying i'm  going to play as nomad  so you 100 will only find me in  the nomad life path it's so cool my god  so this conversation started back in  like 2018  um it was just as i was leaving ign  because of course while working at ign  as a games journalist there is no way  that i would have ever been in any video  game  i did record gears 5 and after party  both in 2018 and my first cyberpunk  session was  in 2019 and then again in early 2020 i  think it was like january this year  maybe so i did do two of those here in  la but yeah the conversation first  started uh back  in in they had a meeting with me in e3  and this is because i had had a  conversation with him about it even  earlier so i don't even know how far  back this goes it might be a while  but yeah at e3 i met with um the guy who  was my quest designer which was very  cool  they did ask me what kind of role that i  wanted to play and at first i was like  can you make me a dj  which is funny because i asked that  before i was a dj in afterparty  they didn't go with that obviously i'm a  nomad in a junkyard here  but yeah they they wrote my quest uh i  had to send them a bunch of  images basically stills so i wasn't  scanned into the game  they just modeled the 3d character based  off of my appearance uh i sent like full  body images  all of that stuff so that they had all  of my features i guess there's even like  i have this little freckle below my  belly button that they actually have on  there  i don't know if that's coincidence but i  do have that it's crazy  and then yeah went and recorded my vo um  some of the toughest vo i've done for  any game  even though the second session was  pretty short i